    "sources": [
      "Field offsets derived from hollow_knight_Data/Managed/Assembly-CSharp.dll metadata by applying Mono's two-pass instance layout (reference-typed fields first), then confirmed against the running game.",
      "Cheat table 'Hollow Knight 1.5.12620 v1.0' by Julia Rosell Saldana, which independently confirms nine of these offsets. It anchors through Mono Data Collector to look up PlayerData._instance by name; this pack finds the same object by layout instead, so it needs nothing injected into the game."
    ],
    "verified": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "build": "Unity 6000.0.61f1"
    },
    "notes": "Anchored on the PlayerData singleton, identified by three values that are game constants rather than save state: max soul 99, reserve cap 99, and 33 soul per Focus. They sit within 40 bytes of each other so they seed the scan directly; over 2 GB of heap only two candidates survived to be checked and one matched. profile_id and play_time then separate the loaded save from the empty template PlayerData that also lives on the heap and is otherwise identical. Geo would not separate them, because a fresh save legitimately has none."
  }
